1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:04,796
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:10,719 --> 00:00:12,679
[ominous music playing]

3
00:00:12,762 --> 00:00:14,264
[Emilia] <i>He can't come back yet.</i>

4
00:00:14,347 --> 00:00:15,932
<i>I don't want to be his slave.</i>

5
00:00:16,016 --> 00:00:18,101
<i>I understand you, Emilia.</i>

6
00:00:18,184 --> 00:00:20,437
<i>I don't want you</i>
<i>to go through the same thing</i>

7
00:00:20,520 --> 00:00:22,772
<i>my sister did with Julio.</i>

8
00:00:22,856 --> 00:00:25,108
[Emilia] <i>Senator Pablo spoke to me.</i>

9
00:00:25,191 --> 00:00:27,152
[in English] <i>And it's final,</i>
<i>I'm running for Senate.</i>

10
00:00:27,235 --> 00:00:29,195
[Ivy] <i>I have to stop Emilia.</i>

11
00:00:29,279 --> 00:00:32,157
<i>I can't let her run for senator,</i>
<i>because if she wins,</i>

12
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:34,826
<i>she'll have the power to manipulate</i>
<i>our judicial system.</i>

13
00:00:34,909 --> 00:00:36,828
[Jepoy] <i>Arthur's recovering safely.</i>

14
00:00:36,911 --> 00:00:38,371
<i>We already have Tonio too.</i>

15
00:00:38,455 --> 00:00:40,665
<i>But I need more whistleblowers</i>

16
00:00:40,749 --> 00:00:41,875
<i>against Emilia.</i>

17
00:00:41,958 --> 00:00:43,918
<i>Butchoy has a love letter for you.</i>

18
00:00:44,002 --> 00:00:45,628
-[Ivy] <i>Butchoy is so cute.</i>
<i>-Um…</i>

19
00:00:45,712 --> 00:00:47,464
<i>I guess I've got more competition now.</i>

20
00:00:47,547 --> 00:00:49,340
[Ivy] <i>You know,</i>
<i>love is just a distraction</i>

21
00:00:49,424 --> 00:00:50,967
<i>from important things.</i>

22
00:00:51,050 --> 00:00:53,261
[in English]<i> I want you</i>
<i>to support Arnaldo.</i>

23
00:00:53,344 --> 00:00:55,638
[Ivy in English] <i>Arnaldo and Emilia.</i>

24
00:00:55,722 --> 00:00:57,682
<i>You want to pit the son</i>
<i>against his mother?</i>

25
00:00:57,766 --> 00:01:01,853
[in English] <i>Competitions like this</i>
<i>produce good results.</i>

26
00:01:01,936 --> 00:01:04,022
[in English] <i>Ms. Aguas,</i>
<i>I was born to lead.</i>

27
00:01:04,105 --> 00:01:05,356
<i>And this is my chance.</i>

28
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:08,026
<i>I'd rather support Emilia</i>

29
00:01:08,109 --> 00:01:09,110
<i>than you.</i>

30
00:01:09,194 --> 00:01:11,029
[in English] <i>What can I do</i>
<i>to change your mind?</i>

31
00:01:11,112 --> 00:01:12,655
<i>The farmers' land.</i>

32
00:01:12,739 --> 00:01:15,408
<i>Are you doing this</i>
<i>for the farmers or for Diego?</i>

33
00:01:15,492 --> 00:01:17,535
[Ivy] <i>It's not my fault if your brother</i>

34
00:01:17,619 --> 00:01:20,330
<i>moves faster than you do.</i>

35
00:01:20,413 --> 00:01:21,790
[Emilia in English] <i>The support</i>
<i>you promised</i>

36
00:01:21,873 --> 00:01:22,832
<i>for my father's candidacy.</i>

37
00:01:22,916 --> 00:01:24,334
<i>Where's the money? Give it to me.</i>

38
00:01:24,417 --> 00:01:27,962
<i>I said I'd support your father, not you.</i>

39
00:01:28,046 --> 00:01:29,506
<i>What newspaper is that?</i>

40
00:01:29,589 --> 00:01:31,341
[Belen] <i>It has a picture of a woman.</i>

41
00:01:31,424 --> 00:01:34,385
<i>Her name is Ivy Aguas.</i>

42
00:01:34,469 --> 00:01:35,762
<i>She's really interested in it.</i>

43
00:01:35,845 --> 00:01:37,680
<i>She keeps looking at it.</i>

44
00:01:40,016 --> 00:01:41,142
Who were you talking to, Raul?

45
00:01:41,226 --> 00:01:43,228
[tense music playing]

46
00:01:44,354 --> 00:01:45,480
It was just my aunt.

47
00:01:46,105 --> 00:01:47,273
Really?

48
00:01:47,899 --> 00:01:50,527
I thought it was the mistress
Emilia was telling me about.

49
00:01:53,321 --> 00:01:54,989
She told me to keep an eye on you.

50
00:02:00,787 --> 00:02:03,289
You know, Auntie,
I think it'd be better if…

51
00:02:04,624 --> 00:02:06,876
you stayed out of our problems.

52
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:08,253
[scoffs]

53
00:02:08,336 --> 00:02:09,420
Raul…

54
00:02:10,296 --> 00:02:13,091
I don't plan on arguing with you.

55
00:02:13,675 --> 00:02:15,009
[in English] The truth is,

56
00:02:15,093 --> 00:02:17,053
I want you and Emilia to sort things out.

57
00:02:17,137 --> 00:02:20,765
For this family,
and for my niece's reputation.

58
00:02:20,849 --> 00:02:22,725
You owe her everything, Raul.

59
00:02:23,768 --> 00:02:25,937
[in English] You won't have anything
if not for her.

60
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:26,938
[in English] So, if I were you,

61
00:02:27,981 --> 00:02:30,650
Don't wait for her to lose
whatever love she feels for you.

62
00:02:32,443 --> 00:02:34,112
Well, I'm not scared of Emilia.

63
00:02:34,779 --> 00:02:36,156
And just so you know,

64
00:02:36,990 --> 00:02:39,200
our relationship's been dead
for a long time now.

65
00:02:39,284 --> 00:02:42,162
[tense music playing]

66
00:02:49,168 --> 00:02:50,086
Hey, girl.

67
00:02:50,169 --> 00:02:51,880
Do you know what happened
to your favorite client?

68
00:02:51,963 --> 00:02:52,797
Of course.

69
00:02:52,881 --> 00:02:55,341
Yesterday, she confronted
her husband's mistress,

70
00:02:55,425 --> 00:02:57,969
[in English] who, by the way,
was his business partner!

71
00:02:58,052 --> 00:03:01,139
Unbelievable.
Snakes these days act like rats.

72
00:03:01,222 --> 00:03:03,766
They'll dig into any holes
just to get what they want.

73
00:03:03,850 --> 00:03:05,018
Exactly.

74
00:03:05,101 --> 00:03:08,021
[in English] I shouldn't have left Arnaldo
with that girl, Ivy.

75
00:03:08,104 --> 00:03:08,980
Ouch!

76
00:03:09,063 --> 00:03:10,398
[in English] Can you watch
what you're doing?

77
00:03:10,481 --> 00:03:12,692
-[in English] I'm sorry, ma'am.
-Sorry?

78
00:03:12,775 --> 00:03:14,402
[in English] I can get you fired,
you know?

79
00:03:15,653 --> 00:03:16,863
Forget it.

80
00:03:17,822 --> 00:03:20,742
[ominous music playing]

81
00:03:26,247 --> 00:03:29,667
[suspenseful music playing]

82
00:03:34,756 --> 00:03:36,007
Raul?

83
00:03:37,675 --> 00:03:38,551
[in English] What's that?

84
00:03:38,635 --> 00:03:39,719
Um…

85
00:03:43,514 --> 00:03:45,016
[tense music playing]

86
00:03:45,099 --> 00:03:46,226
Ivy, again?

87
00:03:49,854 --> 00:03:52,190
-What's your problem, Emilia?
-You!

88
00:03:52,273 --> 00:03:54,817
Everyone in this house is my problem!

89
00:03:54,901 --> 00:03:56,361
[in English] You're all
keeping secrets from me!

90
00:03:56,444 --> 00:03:57,403
What?

91
00:03:57,487 --> 00:03:59,239
How can I keep a secret

92
00:03:59,322 --> 00:04:01,199
when you're keeping me
locked up in this house?

93
00:04:01,282 --> 00:04:03,451
And I will keep you locked here

94
00:04:03,534 --> 00:04:05,286
until you dump your mistress.

95
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:07,205
What are you talking about?
I don't have any mistresses.

96
00:04:07,288 --> 00:04:08,164
Stop this, Emilia.

97
00:04:08,248 --> 00:04:09,415
Okay, Raul.

98
00:04:09,499 --> 00:04:12,418
If it's true you don't have
any other women…

99
00:04:14,003 --> 00:04:15,296
then kneel before me.

100
00:04:16,714 --> 00:04:19,467
Kiss my feet, and say you love me.

101
00:04:19,550 --> 00:04:21,511
[tense music playing]

102
00:04:29,018 --> 00:04:30,019
See?

103
00:04:30,103 --> 00:04:31,562
[in English] You're lying!

104
00:04:31,646 --> 00:04:33,022
[in English] You're lying again!

105
00:04:33,606 --> 00:04:35,483
Why do I even put up with this?

106
00:04:37,652 --> 00:04:38,611
[in English] Please…

107
00:04:39,279 --> 00:04:40,822
Don't give me anymore reasons.

108
00:04:40,905 --> 00:04:42,115
[in English] Don't push me.

109
00:04:43,825 --> 00:04:46,119
[in English] Piece of advice,
Raul, from your wife.

110
00:04:46,911 --> 00:04:49,747
If you're getting bored
just staying in this house…

111
00:04:50,707 --> 00:04:53,042
then you should just serve me.

112
00:04:56,337 --> 00:04:57,463
[Natalie] Hi, Auntie!

113
00:04:58,840 --> 00:05:00,550
-Natalie.
-Uh…

114
00:05:00,633 --> 00:05:02,343
[in English] I'm so sorry to barge in.

115
00:05:04,053 --> 00:05:05,847
[in English] I've been looking
for Arnaldo.

116
00:05:05,930 --> 00:05:07,390
Is he here?

117
00:05:07,473 --> 00:05:09,392
[in English] I checked in his office
and he wasn't there.

118
00:05:09,475 --> 00:05:11,060
[in English] And last I checked.

119
00:05:11,144 --> 00:05:11,978
He was with Ivy.

120
00:05:15,273 --> 00:05:16,649
[in English] Natalie, tell me.

121
00:05:17,942 --> 00:05:20,278
[in English] Is he being considered
by the party to run for Senate?

122
00:05:20,361 --> 00:05:21,654
Um…

123
00:05:22,989 --> 00:05:23,823
[in English] Yes, he is.

124
00:05:25,450 --> 00:05:26,993
[in English] I thought you already knew.

125
00:05:27,076 --> 00:05:29,370
[tense music playing]

126
00:05:38,713 --> 00:05:40,256
-[suspenseful music playing]
-[man grunts]

127
00:05:46,012 --> 00:05:47,138
[cocks gun]

128
00:05:49,766 --> 00:05:51,476
-Tonio.
-No! No!

129
00:05:51,559 --> 00:05:54,228
Please don't!

130
00:05:54,312 --> 00:05:55,271
Out!

131
00:05:55,354 --> 00:05:57,899
You need to calm down a little, dude.

132
00:05:57,982 --> 00:05:58,858
Here, cool down.

133
00:06:00,401 --> 00:06:02,236
Your happy days are over, Tonio.

134
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:04,530
It's time for you to talk.

135
00:06:05,782 --> 00:06:06,616
Take it easy.

136
00:06:07,325 --> 00:06:10,161
Just let me get out of here for a while.

137
00:06:10,745 --> 00:06:12,872
And I swear I'll tell you
everything I know.

138
00:06:14,248 --> 00:06:15,124
Bastard!

139
00:06:15,208 --> 00:06:16,375
Go ahead!

140
00:06:16,459 --> 00:06:17,627
Put it down.

141
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:20,505
I'm already fed up with you.

142
00:06:21,798 --> 00:06:24,467
What if I torture you
until you croak like a frog?

143
00:06:24,550 --> 00:06:26,219
[tense music playing]

144
00:06:42,110 --> 00:06:45,738
[in English] Is this from your
personal account, Ms. Ivy?

145
00:06:45,822 --> 00:06:46,823
[in English] Yes.

146
00:06:47,490 --> 00:06:51,244
I'm buying that property
for personal reasons.

147
00:06:51,327 --> 00:06:53,830
Good thing it's still up
for public auction.

148
00:06:53,913 --> 00:06:57,792
Apparently, the family who owned
this property are all dead.

149
00:06:58,626 --> 00:07:01,754
Joan, as soon as you get the deed of sale,

150
00:07:01,838 --> 00:07:03,923
secure the property immediately.

151
00:07:04,757 --> 00:07:05,883
[in English] Yes, Ms. Aguas.

152
00:07:06,467 --> 00:07:07,343
I will.

153
00:07:11,222 --> 00:07:13,224
Ivy, the mayor's here.

154
00:07:16,060 --> 00:07:17,186
-[in English] We're fine, Nanny.
-Thank you.

155
00:07:17,270 --> 00:07:18,563
[in English] Ms. Aguas.

156
00:07:19,188 --> 00:07:20,731
[clears throat] Mr. Mayor.

157
00:07:20,815 --> 00:07:23,192
[pensive music playing]

158
00:07:26,529 --> 00:07:28,781
[in English] I'm a man of my word,
Ms. Aguas.

159
00:07:28,865 --> 00:07:29,699
TRANSFER CERTIFICATE OF TITLE
IVY AGUAS, OF LEGAL AGE, FILIPINO

160
00:07:29,782 --> 00:07:31,075
I hope you are too.

161
00:07:35,663 --> 00:07:40,501
I can see you really want
to win your prize.

162
00:07:41,502 --> 00:07:42,670
Well, not just that.

163
00:07:44,338 --> 00:07:46,883
I want you to support my senate bid…

164
00:07:48,050 --> 00:07:48,968
Instead of my mom's.

165
00:07:50,094 --> 00:07:51,345
[in English] That's why
I brought this with me.

166
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:56,642
[in English] Stated there is the support
I need from you,

167
00:07:56,726 --> 00:07:58,144
[in English] starting from the campaign,

168
00:07:58,227 --> 00:08:00,438
[in English] up to the moment
of my proclamation.

169
00:08:04,066 --> 00:08:05,651
[in English] Mr. Mayor…

170
00:08:11,782 --> 00:08:13,159
One at a time.

171
00:08:13,242 --> 00:08:15,369
[sensual music playing]

172
00:08:29,592 --> 00:08:30,968
Diego, why are you here?

173
00:08:31,052 --> 00:08:32,553
Um, is Ivy home?

174
00:08:32,637 --> 00:08:34,180
She's inside, talking to the mayor.

175
00:08:34,263 --> 00:08:35,723
Do you want to come in?

176
00:08:35,806 --> 00:08:38,851
[sensual music continues playing]

177
00:08:40,019 --> 00:08:42,313
[in English] You forget that I'm a hunter,
Ms. Aguas.

178
00:08:42,396 --> 00:08:44,732
[in English] I'm not satisfied
with just one catch.

179
00:08:48,277 --> 00:08:49,904
[in English] Mr. Mayor.

180
00:08:51,656 --> 00:08:54,200
Why can't you just let me?

181
00:08:56,077 --> 00:08:58,621
-[Carlotta] Uh…
-It's all right.

182
00:09:03,417 --> 00:09:05,169
I'll be going now. Excuse me. Thanks.

183
00:09:06,379 --> 00:09:07,713
-[in English] Excuse me.
-Yes?

184
00:09:07,797 --> 00:09:09,465
-[in English] Is Arnaldo here?
-Uh…

185
00:09:10,633 --> 00:09:12,927
-Wait, he's…
-[Natalie] Arnaldo!

186
00:09:14,095 --> 00:09:16,097
-[Carlotta] Oh!
-Arnaldo!

187
00:09:18,057 --> 00:09:20,810
[Natalie in English] You're such a bitch,
aren't you?

188
00:09:20,893 --> 00:09:23,354
You just won't stop flirting
with my boyfriend, will you?

189
00:09:24,355 --> 00:09:25,273
-Well?
-Natalie.

190
00:09:25,356 --> 00:09:27,900
-[Arnaldo] Natalie.
-You're such a flirt!

191
00:09:27,984 --> 00:09:29,193
-You bitch!
-Natalie!

192
00:09:29,277 --> 00:09:31,862
[tense music playing]

193
00:09:39,579 --> 00:09:41,872
[Natalie screaming, gasping]

194
00:09:45,585 --> 00:09:48,129
[tense music continues playing]

195
00:09:48,212 --> 00:09:50,506
[whimpering]

196
00:09:55,136 --> 00:09:56,053
[Arnaldo in English] Come here.

197
00:10:05,771 --> 00:10:07,148
[Arnaldo in English] Give me your hand.

198
00:10:07,231 --> 00:10:09,025
[in English] Come on. Come here.

199
00:10:10,318 --> 00:10:12,737
-Don't touch me!
-Natalie.

200
00:10:12,820 --> 00:10:14,155
-Natalie.
-What's wrong with you?

201
00:10:15,823 --> 00:10:16,782
[in English] I'm warning you.

202
00:10:16,866 --> 00:10:18,659
Stay away from my boyfriend.

203
00:10:19,577 --> 00:10:20,703
We aren't doing anything.

204
00:10:20,786 --> 00:10:21,621
[in English] Liar!

205
00:10:21,704 --> 00:10:23,789
Enough! What's wrong with you?

206
00:10:23,873 --> 00:10:26,584
I came here to give her
the title of the farmers' land.

207
00:10:26,667 --> 00:10:29,086
[in English] To convince her to support
my senatorial bid!

208
00:10:30,254 --> 00:10:31,839
You shouldn't argue with her!

209
00:10:32,715 --> 00:10:33,633
[in English] I don't care.

210
00:10:35,635 --> 00:10:36,469
[in English] I don't care!

211
00:10:37,428 --> 00:10:38,471
[in English] From now on.

212
00:10:38,554 --> 00:10:41,682
[in English] I forbid you
to see this woman.

213
00:10:43,768 --> 00:10:45,519
[in English] Or else I'm going
to tell my dad.

214
00:10:47,855 --> 00:10:49,106
Choose.

215
00:10:49,190 --> 00:10:50,399
Ivy,

216
00:10:51,442 --> 00:10:55,821
[in English] or my daddy's support
for your senatorial ambition.

217
00:10:57,865 --> 00:10:59,158
-Natalie…
-Choose!

218
00:11:00,576 --> 00:11:03,079
[tense music playing]

219
00:11:03,913 --> 00:11:05,122
[exasperated sigh]

220
00:11:06,290 --> 00:11:07,333
Natalie.

221
00:11:08,250 --> 00:11:11,003
Let's talk. Natalie!

222
00:11:13,464 --> 00:11:16,300
That Natalie is so scary.

223
00:11:16,384 --> 00:11:18,344
It's a good thing Diego was here.

224
00:11:19,178 --> 00:11:21,806
-I'm fine, Nanny.
-[sighs]

225
00:11:21,889 --> 00:11:22,890
Thank you, Diego.

226
00:11:24,433 --> 00:11:25,476
It's nothing.

227
00:11:25,559 --> 00:11:27,895
Wait, why are you here?

228
00:11:30,022 --> 00:11:31,899
["Sa'Yo" instrumental playing]

229
00:11:32,900 --> 00:11:34,568
I just wanted to give you this.

230
00:11:39,448 --> 00:11:41,450
I have to do something inside.

231
00:11:41,534 --> 00:11:43,285
I'll leave you two there.

232
00:11:49,250 --> 00:11:50,418
Do you remember those flowers?

233
00:11:51,544 --> 00:11:53,254
They're the same ones I gave you

234
00:11:53,337 --> 00:11:55,005
when I first saw you after the contest.

235
00:11:58,509 --> 00:11:59,593
Thank you.

236
00:12:02,596 --> 00:12:04,557
About what Arnaldo said earlier…

237
00:12:05,391 --> 00:12:06,809
about the farmers' land…

238
00:12:08,436 --> 00:12:09,395
Was that true?

239
00:12:11,897 --> 00:12:13,524
Ivy, why are you doing this?

240
00:12:17,528 --> 00:12:18,571
[Ivy sighs]

241
00:12:20,239 --> 00:12:22,116
They are the rightful owners of that land.

242
00:12:22,199 --> 00:12:25,035
It was donated to them long ago.

243
00:12:25,119 --> 00:12:28,164
I just want to do the right thing

244
00:12:28,247 --> 00:12:31,041
and give them back what's theirs.

245
00:12:34,211 --> 00:12:35,588
Ivy, thank you.

246
00:12:36,714 --> 00:12:38,007
Thank you so much!

247
00:12:41,677 --> 00:12:42,845
[in English] Thank you.

248
00:12:45,681 --> 00:12:46,807
I'm sorry.

249
00:12:47,683 --> 00:12:48,976
I just got carried away.

250
00:12:50,394 --> 00:12:52,897
The farmers will be thrilled
when they hear about this!

251
00:12:56,233 --> 00:12:57,902
Thank you.

252
00:12:57,985 --> 00:13:01,322
["Sa'Yo" instrumental continues playing]

253
00:13:11,373 --> 00:13:12,458
[Arnaldo] Natalie!

254
00:13:12,541 --> 00:13:14,543
-Natalie, come on. Let's talk.
-Stop it, Arnaldo!

255
00:13:14,627 --> 00:13:16,295
You don't need to tell the senator on me.

256
00:13:16,378 --> 00:13:17,338
Calm down!

257
00:13:17,421 --> 00:13:19,590
[in English] Stop talking to me!

258
00:13:20,424 --> 00:13:21,717
[in English] And go to hell.

259
00:13:21,800 --> 00:13:24,261
[in English] I'm sorry, okay? I'm sorry.

260
00:13:25,262 --> 00:13:28,015
It's a good thing your mom
told me where you were.

261
00:13:29,475 --> 00:13:31,101
You know what you deserve?

262
00:13:32,561 --> 00:13:34,980
You need to be taught a lesson.

263
00:13:36,690 --> 00:13:38,359
[in English] That's why I'm telling
my dad to remove you

264
00:13:38,442 --> 00:13:39,735
[in English] from the senatorial list,

265
00:13:39,818 --> 00:13:41,529
so you'll learn

266
00:13:41,612 --> 00:13:45,824
you can't have everything you want!

267
00:13:48,911 --> 00:13:51,413
-[in English] Natalie, come on.
-[screams] Don't touch me!

268
00:13:52,748 --> 00:13:54,208
[in English] Go!

269
00:13:55,292 --> 00:13:56,669
[in English] Just go.

270
00:13:57,294 --> 00:13:58,587
[in English] Go!

271
00:13:59,588 --> 00:14:01,090
[in English] Go!

272
00:14:05,970 --> 00:14:08,389
[in English] I hate you!

273
00:14:08,472 --> 00:14:10,516
[heavy breathing]

274
00:14:12,977 --> 00:14:16,146
[whimpering]

275
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:21,944
[Arnaldo] Mom!

276
00:14:22,611 --> 00:14:24,405
Why did you let Natalie go see Ivy?

277
00:14:25,489 --> 00:14:26,323
She was looking for you.

278
00:14:26,407 --> 00:14:27,408
[in English] I thought you'd be with Ivy.

279
00:14:27,491 --> 00:14:28,909
[in English] Don't play dumb with me.

280
00:14:28,993 --> 00:14:29,910
I know you did it on purpose.

281
00:14:29,994 --> 00:14:31,328
You knew I'd go to Ivy

282
00:14:31,412 --> 00:14:34,164
and ask for her endorsement
to replace Grandpa.

283
00:14:34,248 --> 00:14:35,583
[in English] Now that Natalie's mad at me,

284
00:14:35,666 --> 00:14:37,293
[in English] her father's also mad at me!

285
00:14:37,376 --> 00:14:39,086
[in English] There goes my chance
against you.

286
00:14:39,169 --> 00:14:40,212
[clapping furiously]

287
00:14:41,005 --> 00:14:43,549
[in English] Well played! I didn't think
you could be so selfish!

288
00:14:46,927 --> 00:14:49,680
[in English] How dare you talk
to me that way?

289
00:14:49,763 --> 00:14:51,015
You're the one who's selfish.

290
00:14:51,724 --> 00:14:55,269
You think I don't know
you gave the farmers' land title to Ivy?

291
00:14:55,352 --> 00:14:56,186
So, what?

292
00:14:56,270 --> 00:14:58,606
I have every right to use that
because it's under my name!

293
00:14:59,273 --> 00:15:01,275
[in English] I have every right
to use that

294
00:15:01,358 --> 00:15:02,902
to help me with my political ambitions!

295
00:15:02,985 --> 00:15:04,820
Why are you so selfish?

296
00:15:04,904 --> 00:15:06,864
Have you forgotten that we're a family?

297
00:15:06,947 --> 00:15:09,783
We should help each other
instead of going against one another!

298
00:15:09,867 --> 00:15:11,243
[tense music playing]

299
00:15:12,077 --> 00:15:13,495
Arnaldo.

300
00:15:16,123 --> 00:15:19,543
[in English] I know your grandfather
groomed you to follow in his footsteps.

301
00:15:20,294 --> 00:15:21,503
But you're still young.

302
00:15:22,254 --> 00:15:24,340
You have your future ahead of you.

303
00:15:24,423 --> 00:15:26,467
You can still prove your worth.

304
00:15:28,594 --> 00:15:30,054
[in English] This is my time.

305
00:15:31,096 --> 00:15:33,057
[in English] This is my last chance

306
00:15:33,140 --> 00:15:35,142
[in English] to prove my worth
to your grandpa.

307
00:15:35,893 --> 00:15:37,561
[in English] Don't steal it from me.

308
00:15:37,645 --> 00:15:40,230
[suspenseful music playing]

309
00:15:41,398 --> 00:15:42,524
Arnaldo.

310
00:15:46,362 --> 00:15:49,865
[in English] Please, give this to me.

311
00:15:49,949 --> 00:15:52,785
[sobbing]

312
00:15:55,621 --> 00:15:56,830
[sniffles]

313
00:15:57,373 --> 00:16:00,793
[in English] Do you want me
to get the land title back from Ivy?

314
00:16:00,876 --> 00:16:04,004
[suspenseful music continues playing]

315
00:16:07,424 --> 00:16:10,260
[in English] No need. I have a plan.

316
00:16:11,804 --> 00:16:12,721
[exhales]

317
00:16:14,098 --> 00:16:14,932
[in English] Thank you.

318
00:16:15,015 --> 00:16:18,227
[in English] You're the best son
any mother could ever ask for.

319
00:16:18,936 --> 00:16:20,896
[sighs in relief]

320
00:16:22,064 --> 00:16:25,484
[ominous music playing]

321
00:16:27,027 --> 00:16:30,114
It's ours. This land is ours!

322
00:16:30,197 --> 00:16:32,616
Everyone! Thank you very much.

323
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:34,326
We are indebted to you.

324
00:16:34,410 --> 00:16:38,414
Ever since the dispersal,
you've really helped us out.

325
00:16:38,497 --> 00:16:40,165
-That's right.
-Exactly.

326
00:16:40,249 --> 00:16:42,126
-You're welcome, Mr. Fernan.
-Thank you, Ms. Ivy.

327
00:16:42,209 --> 00:16:46,880
The truth is, it's yours.
The land is yours.

328
00:16:46,964 --> 00:16:48,215
I just did what's right

329
00:16:48,298 --> 00:16:50,300
and gave back the title to you.

330
00:16:50,384 --> 00:16:51,760
-Thank you so much!
-Thank you!

331
00:16:51,844 --> 00:16:52,886
Thank you very much.

332
00:16:52,970 --> 00:16:55,222
-Thank you.
-[applauding]

333
00:16:55,305 --> 00:16:56,306
Ms. Beautiful!

334
00:16:57,850 --> 00:16:59,059
This is for you,

335
00:16:59,143 --> 00:17:01,311
so you'll always remember
how thankful we are.

336
00:17:01,895 --> 00:17:03,856
-[woman] Wow.
-[man] Nice.

337
00:17:03,939 --> 00:17:05,566
[in English] Thank you, Butchoy.

338
00:17:06,525 --> 00:17:08,318
Ms. Beautiful, can I have a kiss?

339
00:17:08,402 --> 00:17:11,196
[everyone gasps and laughs]

340
00:17:13,449 --> 00:17:14,283
Of course, you can!

341
00:17:14,366 --> 00:17:17,745
[cheering and applause]

342
00:17:17,828 --> 00:17:19,163
-You're so cute!
-[man] Oh, wow.

343
00:17:19,246 --> 00:17:21,123
You're so cute, Butchoy.

344
00:17:22,833 --> 00:17:26,253
[tender music playing]

345
00:17:30,090 --> 00:17:30,966
-[man] Let's try it.
-[laughter]

346
00:17:31,050 --> 00:17:32,885
-[man] The other side.
-[woman] Cat got his tongue. Look.

347
00:17:32,968 --> 00:17:35,554
[laughing]

348
00:17:37,890 --> 00:17:39,224
[cheering and applause]

349
00:17:40,017 --> 00:17:42,853
[in English] Governor, I've set
your lunch date with Judge Rivas

350
00:17:42,936 --> 00:17:45,773
[in English] and Mrs. Segovia
of the Land Registration Authority.

351
00:17:45,856 --> 00:17:46,899
[in English] Good.

352
00:17:48,192 --> 00:17:49,526
[in English] Can you please call up Ivy?

353
00:17:49,610 --> 00:17:51,945
Tell her I have what she needs.

354
00:17:52,571 --> 00:17:53,781
Will do, Madam.

355
00:17:53,864 --> 00:17:58,035
[ominous music playing]

356
00:18:09,505 --> 00:18:11,882
-[knocking on door]
-[door opens]

357
00:18:14,134 --> 00:18:18,013
[in English] Hey.
What are these flowers for?

358
00:18:24,394 --> 00:18:26,146
[in English] I don't want to talk to you.

359
00:18:26,230 --> 00:18:27,356
Natalie.

360
00:18:30,067 --> 00:18:32,861
[in English] Come on, please understand.
I need to do those things.

361
00:18:34,238 --> 00:18:35,364
You need to flirt with her?

362
00:18:36,615 --> 00:18:39,284
[in English] Arnaldo, I don't think so.

363
00:18:39,368 --> 00:18:40,536
[in English] It's a political strategy.

364
00:18:40,619 --> 00:18:41,995
Your father does it too.

365
00:18:44,540 --> 00:18:45,833
Even so.

366
00:18:47,334 --> 00:18:48,877
[in English] I thought you'd be different.

367
00:18:51,255 --> 00:18:52,506
[in English] I am different.

368
00:18:57,594 --> 00:19:00,806
[quiet music playing]

369
00:19:00,889 --> 00:19:01,807
[in English] Prove it.

370
00:19:01,890 --> 00:19:05,519
[sensual music playing]

371
00:19:18,532 --> 00:19:20,993
[exhales]

372
00:19:21,076 --> 00:19:23,579
[sensual music continues playing]

373
00:19:29,626 --> 00:19:33,922
So, I'll get going.
I have a lot to take care of.

374
00:19:34,006 --> 00:19:36,758
Thank you again. Take care, Ms. Ivy!

375
00:19:36,842 --> 00:19:39,761
[townsfolk] Thank you for your help,
Ms. Ivy.

376
00:19:40,846 --> 00:19:43,891
Ms. Ivy, I'm sorry,
but our car broke down.

377
00:19:43,974 --> 00:19:45,601
The fan belt got snipped again.

378
00:19:45,684 --> 00:19:48,604
We need to have it towed back to the shop.

379
00:19:49,188 --> 00:19:51,023
-It's broken again?
-Yes.

380
00:19:51,732 --> 00:19:54,943
Okay. I'll just call someone to tow it.

381
00:19:55,027 --> 00:19:57,112
-Okay, ma'am.
-Can I…

382
00:19:57,196 --> 00:19:58,739
-Of course!
-Sure! Please sit down.

383
00:19:58,822 --> 00:20:00,407
We'll call for you!

384
00:20:00,490 --> 00:20:02,075
Uh, Ivy, I'll drive you home.

385
00:20:03,160 --> 00:20:05,245
If it's all right with you.

386
00:20:05,329 --> 00:20:07,331
[man] Let him drive you home, ma'am.

387
00:20:07,414 --> 00:20:08,457
You should let him, ma'am.

388
00:20:08,540 --> 00:20:11,919
So, you're driving her home now, huh?

389
00:20:12,753 --> 00:20:14,713
Oh, that depends on Butchoy.

390
00:20:14,796 --> 00:20:17,841
-[man] Come on. Let her.
-Let her.

391
00:20:17,925 --> 00:20:20,010
-[woman] What can you say, Butchoy?
-[man] Is it okay?

392
00:20:20,093 --> 00:20:22,763
Is it okay if Diego drives me home?

393
00:20:22,846 --> 00:20:27,434
Yes, Butchoy, let him drive her home.

394
00:20:27,517 --> 00:20:28,977
Okay.

395
00:20:29,061 --> 00:20:31,271
[upbeat music playing]

396
00:20:36,652 --> 00:20:39,488
[soft music playing]

397
00:21:06,723 --> 00:21:10,978
[sentimental music playing]

398
00:21:21,405 --> 00:21:23,490
That's my best friend's favorite toy.

399
00:21:32,457 --> 00:21:35,294
I know some places here in Ardiente…

400
00:21:35,377 --> 00:21:36,461
that are really peaceful.

401
00:21:38,547 --> 00:21:42,009
If you want, we can check them out.

402
00:21:42,092 --> 00:21:45,053
[sentimental music continues playing]

403
00:21:47,764 --> 00:21:48,974
Really?

404
00:21:51,393 --> 00:21:52,644
Let's go.

405
00:22:01,611 --> 00:22:03,447
[engine rumbling]

406
00:22:10,495 --> 00:22:15,709
[tender music playing]

407
00:22:20,005 --> 00:22:21,214
What are we doing here?

408
00:22:22,299 --> 00:22:26,303
Didn't I say I'd bring you somewhere
a little more peaceful?

409
00:22:26,386 --> 00:22:29,097
[birds cawing]

410
00:22:30,265 --> 00:22:31,475
Come on!

411
00:22:31,558 --> 00:22:34,352
[tender music continues playing]

412
00:22:36,605 --> 00:22:37,564
Ivy!

413
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:51,369
This is going to be our new home!

414
00:22:56,416 --> 00:22:57,501
[exhales]

415
00:22:58,585 --> 00:22:59,628
[Diego] Ivy!

416
00:23:02,631 --> 00:23:03,882
Come here.

417
00:23:10,138 --> 00:23:12,808
This was my best friend Lily's old house.

418
00:23:15,519 --> 00:23:16,520
Actually…

419
00:23:17,229 --> 00:23:20,065
This was where I felt what it was like
to have a happy family.

420
00:23:21,191 --> 00:23:23,693
Lily's parents accepted me for who I am.

421
00:23:24,820 --> 00:23:26,071
No judgment.

422
00:23:28,448 --> 00:23:29,491
Like…

423
00:23:30,534 --> 00:23:32,452
Like a part of their family.

424
00:23:32,536 --> 00:23:35,747
[tender music playing]

425
00:23:44,965 --> 00:23:49,302
[in English] Thank you so much,
Lucy and Helen.

426
00:23:49,386 --> 00:23:51,471
I know how busy you both are,

427
00:23:51,555 --> 00:23:55,183
[in English] but you still entertained
my request to come here.

428
00:23:55,267 --> 00:23:56,560
[in English] It's nothing, Emilia.

429
00:23:56,643 --> 00:23:58,353
Compared to what you've done for me

430
00:23:58,436 --> 00:24:00,147
[in English] to be the town's
provincial judge.

431
00:24:00,230 --> 00:24:01,398
[both chuckle]

432
00:24:01,481 --> 00:24:04,234
[in English] And for making me the head
of the Land Registration Authority.

433
00:24:06,486 --> 00:24:07,779
[in English] So…

434
00:24:07,863 --> 00:24:11,950
[in English] Does that mean you'll give me
the land title I asked for?

435
00:24:12,033 --> 00:24:15,412
[in English] Of course, it's legal
under PD 1529.

436
00:24:16,037 --> 00:24:18,665
We can already transfer
the ownership under your name.

437
00:24:18,748 --> 00:24:20,834
[in English] In fact, I already gave
the court order to Helen.

438
00:24:22,252 --> 00:24:24,379
I had this rushed earlier, Emilia.

439
00:24:24,462 --> 00:24:27,174
Here's the new deed to the land.

440
00:24:27,257 --> 00:24:29,926
[ominous music playing]

441
00:24:31,469 --> 00:24:33,054
TRANSFER CERTIFICATE OF TITLE

442
00:24:33,138 --> 00:24:34,931
EMILIA ARDIENTE TORILLO,
OF LEGAL AGE, FILIPINO

443
00:24:40,687 --> 00:24:43,982
[instrumental theme music playing]

444
00:24:45,150 --> 00:24:46,443
This over here…

445
00:24:48,904 --> 00:24:51,573
used to be the day care center
of Lily's mother.

446
00:24:52,699 --> 00:24:53,992
Teacher Camia.

447
00:25:05,128 --> 00:25:08,340
She was the one who told me
that I could be brave.

448
00:25:09,633 --> 00:25:11,051
That I could be strong.

449
00:25:17,766 --> 00:25:19,517
[Ivy] <i>Mom, what happened to you?</i>

450
00:25:19,601 --> 00:25:20,977
<i>Hey!</i>

451
00:25:21,061 --> 00:25:23,813
<i>Lily… Run!</i>

452
00:25:26,858 --> 00:25:27,984
Ivy.

453
00:25:29,444 --> 00:25:30,528
Are you all right?

454
00:25:33,490 --> 00:25:35,450
Come on, I have something else
I want to show you.

455
00:25:36,117 --> 00:25:37,410
Let's go.

456
00:25:37,494 --> 00:25:38,328
And…

457
00:25:39,537 --> 00:25:43,500
[in English] this is where Lily
and I used to exercise.

458
00:25:43,583 --> 00:25:45,669
[in English] This is where she taught me
how to do jumping jacks

459
00:25:45,752 --> 00:25:47,128
[in English] and use jump ropes.

460
00:25:47,212 --> 00:25:49,923
This is where she made me
run again and again

461
00:25:50,006 --> 00:25:51,800
while carrying my bag.

462
00:25:53,134 --> 00:25:55,387
Uh, can I borrow your bag?

463
00:25:55,929 --> 00:25:57,514
-What?
-Come on, let me borrow it.

464
00:25:59,849 --> 00:26:01,101
This is what she made me do.

465
00:26:02,143 --> 00:26:03,895
She made me carry my bag,

466
00:26:03,979 --> 00:26:05,480
and it was so heavy,

467
00:26:05,563 --> 00:26:08,858
and then she would make me
run around like this.

468
00:26:08,942 --> 00:26:10,360
Whoo!

469
00:26:10,443 --> 00:26:12,487
[young Lily] <i>Ready, set, go!</i>

470
00:26:12,570 --> 00:26:14,030
Hurry! Go, Diego!

471
00:26:14,114 --> 00:26:16,408
Run! Come on, faster!

472
00:26:17,659 --> 00:26:20,287
Just like this. I ran around in circles.

473
00:26:20,370 --> 00:26:23,415
[bright music playing]

474
00:26:23,498 --> 00:26:26,584
Actually, I would get so exhausted

475
00:26:27,168 --> 00:26:28,336
after running just one round.

476
00:26:29,004 --> 00:26:29,963
I'd be panting.

477
00:26:31,006 --> 00:26:33,383
I was so fat, almost as fat as Butchoy.

478
00:26:33,466 --> 00:26:34,926
My stomach was so big…

479
00:26:35,760 --> 00:26:39,514
it was maybe two
or three times bigger then.

480
00:26:41,182 --> 00:26:42,726
[sighs] I can't believe it.

481
00:26:43,643 --> 00:26:45,520
Lily helped me so much.

482
00:26:46,313 --> 00:26:48,982
[tender music playing]

483
00:26:50,358 --> 00:26:51,443
Um…

484
00:26:51,526 --> 00:26:53,695
You're sweating. Can I have my bag?

485
00:26:53,778 --> 00:26:54,696
Oh.

486
00:26:55,280 --> 00:26:56,281
You're…

487
00:27:00,577 --> 00:27:01,661
You're all sweaty. Here.

488
00:27:05,040 --> 00:27:06,041
Wipe it off.

489
00:27:07,709 --> 00:27:08,543
Thanks.

490
00:27:08,626 --> 00:27:11,629
[tender music continues playing]

491
00:27:22,724 --> 00:27:23,725
It's so hot.

492
00:27:29,439 --> 00:27:32,067
Lily was like my personal trainer.

493
00:27:32,150 --> 00:27:34,611
You know, we used to
run circles around these trees.

494
00:27:35,362 --> 00:27:36,446
Just like this.

495
00:27:38,448 --> 00:27:40,992
-Whoo!
-[young Lily] <i>Go Diego, duck!</i>

496
00:27:41,076 --> 00:27:42,786
Just one hand, no cheating!

497
00:27:42,869 --> 00:27:43,828
Go! You can do it!

498
00:27:48,375 --> 00:27:50,168
From here until there.

499
00:27:52,504 --> 00:27:55,256
So that no matter how much I ate,

500
00:27:55,340 --> 00:27:56,633
I wouldn't get fat.

501
00:27:59,511 --> 00:28:02,222
Back then, I thought they were helping me

502
00:28:02,305 --> 00:28:03,598
so my family would accept me.

503
00:28:04,974 --> 00:28:07,727
But the truth was, they were helping me…

504
00:28:09,145 --> 00:28:11,981
so I could get to know,
love, and accept myself.

505
00:28:18,405 --> 00:28:19,531
Your…

506
00:28:21,908 --> 00:28:24,702
Lily? Her name's Lily, right?

507
00:28:27,288 --> 00:28:29,290
She's a big part of your life.

508
00:28:31,626 --> 00:28:35,046
That's probably why I brought you here.

509
00:28:36,089 --> 00:28:37,340
-I… Ouch!
-Oh.

510
00:28:37,424 --> 00:28:38,883
-That hurts!
-Diego.

511
00:28:40,343 --> 00:28:41,553
-Oh! Ouch.
-Diego.

512
00:28:42,220 --> 00:28:44,055
[young Lily] I told you to be careful.

513
00:28:45,724 --> 00:28:46,891
I'm fine.

514
00:28:51,396 --> 00:28:52,522
I can't explain it.

515
00:28:54,232 --> 00:28:57,777
Whenever I'm with you, Ivy…

516
00:29:03,283 --> 00:29:06,578
I feel like I'm with Lily again.

517
00:29:06,661 --> 00:29:09,664
[tender music playing]

518
00:29:21,926 --> 00:29:22,844
Come on.

519
00:29:22,927 --> 00:29:24,637
There's something else I want to show you.

520
00:29:25,972 --> 00:29:28,266
-Is it all right?
-Yeah. It's fine.

521
00:29:28,349 --> 00:29:30,393
It's a bit far from here.

522
00:29:31,352 --> 00:29:33,521
Just watch your step.
It's a bit rocky here.

523
00:29:39,903 --> 00:29:40,862
[in English] Happy?

524
00:29:44,157 --> 00:29:46,743
[in English] I guess you can tell Mom
we're okay now.

525
00:29:48,536 --> 00:29:52,415
[in English] As long as you promise me
that it's just me.

526
00:29:54,083 --> 00:29:55,418
[in English] Just me forever.

527
00:29:56,211 --> 00:29:57,754
[in English] I just don't like it
when we fight.

528
00:29:59,255 --> 00:30:00,089
Me too.

529
00:30:00,173 --> 00:30:02,717
[in English] It's stressful.

530
00:30:03,635 --> 00:30:04,636
That's why…

531
00:30:05,970 --> 00:30:07,972
you should stay away from that woman.

532
00:30:09,808 --> 00:30:12,435
Because if you don't,
I'll lose my patience.

533
00:30:13,102 --> 00:30:15,897
[in English] I just might kill her
with my bare hands.

534
00:30:15,980 --> 00:30:17,190
[tense music playing]

535
00:30:17,273 --> 00:30:20,819
[phone ringing]

536
00:30:21,820 --> 00:30:23,112
[in English] Hello?

537
00:30:23,196 --> 00:30:25,490
Okay. Tell them I'm on my way.

538
00:30:25,573 --> 00:30:27,033
[ominous music playing]

539
00:30:28,326 --> 00:30:31,746
[in English] I have to meet some important
people for my senatorial bid…

540
00:30:32,664 --> 00:30:35,375
[in English] because whether Mom likes it
or not, I will be running for senator.

541
00:30:35,458 --> 00:30:36,334
[ominous music playing]

542
00:30:36,417 --> 00:30:39,379
That's what Grandpa wants,
and that's what'll happen.

543
00:30:39,462 --> 00:30:44,175
[ominous music playing]

544
00:30:44,259 --> 00:30:45,426
Ivy, come on!

545
00:30:46,135 --> 00:30:47,470
This is it!

546
00:30:47,554 --> 00:30:49,556
This is our sanctuary.

547
00:30:49,639 --> 00:30:52,350
This is where we pour out
all our emotions.

548
00:30:52,934 --> 00:30:54,727
All our pain, our sorrows.

549
00:30:54,811 --> 00:30:56,479
You can shout out whatever you feel here.

550
00:30:59,399 --> 00:31:01,776
-Lily, where are you?
-[quiet music playing]

551
00:31:01,860 --> 00:31:04,362
I miss you so much!

552
00:31:06,072 --> 00:31:07,198
Ivy, your turn.

553
00:31:07,866 --> 00:31:08,950
Come on. Shout it out.

554
00:31:10,410 --> 00:31:14,581
Lily, I hope you're happy
wherever you are!

555
00:31:16,749 --> 00:31:17,709
Ivy.

556
00:31:18,668 --> 00:31:22,338
Seriously, it feels so good
after you shout it out.

557
00:31:22,422 --> 00:31:23,631
Come on.

558
00:31:23,715 --> 00:31:26,259
[tender music playing]

559
00:31:27,719 --> 00:31:30,889
[in English] Sorry.
I might be annoying you.

560
00:31:32,515 --> 00:31:34,142
[in English] I just really
miss my best friend.

561
00:31:36,936 --> 00:31:38,897
But I don't think she's ever coming back.

562
00:31:40,481 --> 00:31:41,524
What about you?

563
00:31:42,275 --> 00:31:43,693
[in English] Did you have a best friend
when you were a kid?

564
00:31:43,776 --> 00:31:46,154
[tender music playing]

565
00:31:52,368 --> 00:31:53,453
I was a loner.

566
00:31:55,038 --> 00:31:56,915
I was always cooped up in my room.

567
00:31:57,832 --> 00:31:59,417
All I did was read.

568
00:32:00,919 --> 00:32:03,630
Really? I love to read too.

569
00:32:04,380 --> 00:32:05,798
Just like Lily.

570
00:32:06,382 --> 00:32:07,759
Do you know <i>The Count of Monte Cristo</i>?

571
00:32:12,472 --> 00:32:15,099
[in English] "Moral wounds
have this peculiarity.

572
00:32:16,184 --> 00:32:17,435
[in English] They may be hidden…

573
00:32:19,103 --> 00:32:20,480
[in English] but they never close."

574
00:32:21,648 --> 00:32:25,610
[in English] "Always painful,
always ready to bleed when touched…

575
00:32:26,486 --> 00:32:29,864
[in English] they remain fresh
and open in the heart."

576
00:32:34,702 --> 00:32:36,412
It's an amazing book.

577
00:32:39,582 --> 00:32:41,459
It's about a man…

578
00:32:43,378 --> 00:32:44,420
seeking revenge…

579
00:32:45,380 --> 00:32:48,883
because he was abused
and imprisoned unjustly.

580
00:32:54,430 --> 00:32:55,807
What about you, Diego?

581
00:32:57,100 --> 00:32:58,267
Do you think what he did was right?

582
00:33:00,311 --> 00:33:01,354
No.

583
00:33:02,021 --> 00:33:04,273
Revenge won't get you anywhere.

584
00:33:05,400 --> 00:33:06,359
But…

585
00:33:07,235 --> 00:33:09,445
But what they did to him was cruel.

586
00:33:10,571 --> 00:33:11,572
I understand him.

587
00:33:12,323 --> 00:33:14,575
If I were him,
I'd probably do the same thing.

588
00:33:21,541 --> 00:33:22,709
Uh…

589
00:33:22,792 --> 00:33:24,168
I've shown you almost everything.

590
00:33:25,044 --> 00:33:26,879
The next place I'm going to show you…

591
00:33:27,964 --> 00:33:29,757
is the most special place
for me and my best friend.

592
00:33:30,842 --> 00:33:33,302
Come on. Let's go!

593
00:33:39,809 --> 00:33:42,311
Thank you for accommodating me
on such short notice.

594
00:33:43,312 --> 00:33:44,397
What's this for, Mayor?

595
00:33:44,480 --> 00:33:46,232
Is this about what the governor said

596
00:33:46,315 --> 00:33:48,151
about you not following
in your grandpa's footsteps?

597
00:33:48,234 --> 00:33:49,736
[tense music playing]

598
00:33:49,819 --> 00:33:51,696
You know the governor.
She can be pretty hasty.

599
00:33:52,488 --> 00:33:54,991
We're here because I want
to show you the new site

600
00:33:55,074 --> 00:33:56,242
[in English] for the export
processing zone,

601
00:33:56,909 --> 00:33:58,453
and to tell you that

602
00:33:58,536 --> 00:34:01,414
[in English] I'll be handling
the project from now on.

603
00:34:01,497 --> 00:34:02,832
That's good to hear.

604
00:34:02,915 --> 00:34:06,002
No offense, Mayor, but I find
it hard to trust your mother.

605
00:34:06,961 --> 00:34:08,129
I know.

606
00:34:08,212 --> 00:34:11,090
That's why I want you to inform everyone
about this development,

607
00:34:11,674 --> 00:34:14,177
so we can be sure
that the party chooses me.

608
00:34:15,344 --> 00:34:17,638
-So, shall we?
-You can count on us, Mayor.

609
00:34:20,808 --> 00:34:23,394
Ivy, come on!
This is what I was talking about.

610
00:34:25,563 --> 00:34:27,356
This is the secret garden
Lily and I shared.

611
00:34:27,440 --> 00:34:28,649
Beautiful, isn't it?

612
00:34:29,650 --> 00:34:31,611
When she disappeared, I took care of it.

613
00:34:31,694 --> 00:34:33,237
I tended the flowers,
did some landscaping…

614
00:34:35,073 --> 00:34:37,700
So if she returns,
this is what she'll see.

615
00:34:39,202 --> 00:34:40,411
I'm sure she'll be happy to see this.

616
00:34:41,204 --> 00:34:43,081
This is her favorite place.

617
00:34:44,832 --> 00:34:47,668
But, like I said…

618
00:34:49,670 --> 00:34:50,630
I don't know if she's ever coming back.

619
00:34:52,465 --> 00:34:55,760
I did everything, Ivy. Did you know that…

620
00:34:55,843 --> 00:34:58,805
I even called out for her
on national television?

621
00:34:58,888 --> 00:34:59,806
You really did that?

622
00:35:02,350 --> 00:35:03,518
For Lily?

623
00:35:07,063 --> 00:35:08,981
But it's been 13 years,
and I still haven't seen her.

624
00:35:11,859 --> 00:35:13,486
I hope she's happy wherever she is.

625
00:35:16,197 --> 00:35:18,950
But even if I don't see her again…

626
00:35:21,327 --> 00:35:23,121
she'll always be my best friend.

627
00:35:23,204 --> 00:35:26,833
-[tender music playing]
-[sniffles]

628
00:35:32,505 --> 00:35:34,715
It's a good thing the project
will push through, Mayor.

629
00:35:34,799 --> 00:35:37,051
We admire you
for standing up to your mother,

630
00:35:37,135 --> 00:35:38,344
and for telling her

631
00:35:38,427 --> 00:35:40,888
you're the rightful person
to run for Senate.

632
00:35:40,972 --> 00:35:43,349
I just want to protect my family's name

633
00:35:43,432 --> 00:35:46,477
and everything our party
has done for this town.

634
00:35:46,561 --> 00:35:49,063
I'm sure your grandfather
would be proud of you.

635
00:35:49,147 --> 00:35:50,606
Thanks.

636
00:35:50,690 --> 00:35:51,732
Shall we begin?

637
00:35:51,816 --> 00:35:53,693
I think it's best if we split up.

638
00:35:53,776 --> 00:35:55,153
-[in English] All right, let's go.
-Let's go.

639
00:35:58,489 --> 00:36:02,743
[instrumental theme music playing]

640
00:36:08,249 --> 00:36:09,292
If…

641
00:36:12,003 --> 00:36:13,462
If I were Lily…

642
00:36:16,799 --> 00:36:20,553
I would probably say…

643
00:36:25,933 --> 00:36:27,894
"Diego, you have to move on…

644
00:36:28,895 --> 00:36:30,813
because we lead different lives now.

645
00:36:33,441 --> 00:36:35,443
And I want you to be happy."

646
00:36:35,526 --> 00:36:38,487
[instrumental theme music playing]

647
00:36:44,452 --> 00:36:45,536
I'd say that.

648
00:36:46,621 --> 00:36:49,707
If… If I were Lily.

649
00:36:50,958 --> 00:36:53,252
[suspenseful music playing]

650
00:36:56,797 --> 00:36:58,591
What are they doing here?

651
00:37:15,816 --> 00:37:16,984
-[gunshot]
-[shrieks]

652
00:37:17,068 --> 00:37:17,944
Who's that?

653
00:37:18,653 --> 00:37:19,862
Don't shoot!

654
00:37:21,572 --> 00:37:22,406
Oh, Diego.

655
00:37:24,200 --> 00:37:25,576
It's just me.

656
00:37:26,452 --> 00:37:29,705
I saw an animal, but I missed it.

657
00:37:30,331 --> 00:37:31,540
Arnaldo?

658
00:37:31,624 --> 00:37:33,501
[in English] Sorry, did I interrupt you?

659
00:37:34,043 --> 00:37:35,378
What are you doing here?

660
00:37:35,461 --> 00:37:36,837
I'm showing Ivy around.

661
00:37:37,630 --> 00:37:39,423
Well, I'm showing my friends around too.

662
00:37:39,507 --> 00:37:42,009
I showed them the EPZ's new location.

663
00:37:43,177 --> 00:37:44,428
[in English] And, uh…

664
00:37:46,222 --> 00:37:47,181
[in English] to which I wonder…

665
00:37:47,890 --> 00:37:52,019
why this isn't a part
of the site's new location.

666
00:37:53,062 --> 00:37:54,730
Well, it doesn't matter.

667
00:37:54,814 --> 00:37:57,441
[in English] I have expansion plans,
anyway.

668
00:37:57,525 --> 00:37:59,443
So, say goodbye to this place, Diego.

669
00:38:00,361 --> 00:38:02,196
I have to go.

670
00:38:02,280 --> 00:38:03,447
[in English] Oh, by the way,

671
00:38:03,531 --> 00:38:05,116
Ms. Aguas,

672
00:38:05,199 --> 00:38:06,784
don't forget, you owe me something.

673
00:38:06,867 --> 00:38:09,036
[tense music playing]

674
00:38:11,330 --> 00:38:12,415
No.

675
00:38:12,915 --> 00:38:14,625
I won't let him have this place.

676
00:38:27,722 --> 00:38:30,516
Jasmin? Do you need something?

677
00:38:30,599 --> 00:38:32,852
[somber music playing]

678
00:38:52,496 --> 00:38:54,832
[somber music continues playing]

679
00:39:06,927 --> 00:39:09,430
[tense music plays]

680
00:39:10,306 --> 00:39:12,475
Raul has to know about this.

681
00:39:19,440 --> 00:39:24,195
[tender music playing]

682
00:39:26,113 --> 00:39:27,198
Earlier…

683
00:39:28,699 --> 00:39:31,535
I really wanted to tell him everything.

684
00:39:32,411 --> 00:39:34,330
But then I thought…

685
00:39:35,206 --> 00:39:38,793
what good would it do?

686
00:39:40,795 --> 00:39:41,796
Nothing.

687
00:39:42,755 --> 00:39:44,757
Besides, I'm sure that…

688
00:39:46,634 --> 00:39:48,719
…he'll side with his family.

689
00:39:50,346 --> 00:39:51,514
And…

690
00:39:53,641 --> 00:39:57,395
if he finds out the truth, he'll hate me.

691
00:39:58,479 --> 00:39:59,688
Ivy.

692
00:39:59,772 --> 00:40:01,440
It's better this way.

693
00:40:02,274 --> 00:40:04,693
Just let Lily live in his memory.

694
00:40:08,948 --> 00:40:11,158
Lily is just a memory to me…

695
00:40:14,161 --> 00:40:15,788
and to Diego.

696
00:40:17,706 --> 00:40:20,084
Is that what you really want?

697
00:40:24,422 --> 00:40:25,631
[sniffles]

698
00:40:26,632 --> 00:40:27,675
[exhales]

699
00:40:29,427 --> 00:40:30,344
Ivy.

700
00:40:32,513 --> 00:40:33,597
Nanny, excuse me.

701
00:40:33,681 --> 00:40:38,519
I still have to prepare
for my dinner with Emilia.

702
00:40:38,602 --> 00:40:39,603
Ivy.

703
00:40:40,813 --> 00:40:44,191
Are you sure you're ready to face Emilia?

704
00:40:57,246 --> 00:40:59,248
-[in English] Natalie.
-Yay, I made it.

705
00:40:59,331 --> 00:41:00,207
[in English] Hi, Auntie.

706
00:41:00,291 --> 00:41:01,667
-[in English] Hi.
-Hello.

707
00:41:02,418 --> 00:41:03,878
[in English] Hey, how are you and Arnaldo?

708
00:41:03,961 --> 00:41:06,130
Um… We're actually really good.

709
00:41:06,213 --> 00:41:09,049
That's good.
I hope you don't argue again, okay?

710
00:41:09,133 --> 00:41:12,720
[in English] I know. As long as Ivy
stays out of the picture,

711
00:41:12,803 --> 00:41:13,721
[in English] I guess we'll be fine.

712
00:41:13,804 --> 00:41:16,348
[in English] Then you will have to
guard Arnaldo from Ivy.

713
00:41:17,016 --> 00:41:17,850
[in English] I will.

714
00:41:17,933 --> 00:41:19,185
[in English] That's my daughter-in-law.

715
00:41:19,268 --> 00:41:20,769
Would you like to come with me?

716
00:41:20,853 --> 00:41:21,770
[in English] Sure. Where are we going?

717
00:41:22,480 --> 00:41:24,940
[in English] Some place where you
will witness my greatness.

718
00:41:25,024 --> 00:41:27,151
[in English] I like that. Let's go?

719
00:41:27,776 --> 00:41:28,736
[in English] Let's go.

720
00:41:28,819 --> 00:41:31,572
[ominous music playing]

721
00:41:31,655 --> 00:41:35,367
[in English] Well, I called up this
meeting to correct some mistakes.

722
00:41:36,619 --> 00:41:37,745
What mistakes?

723
00:41:38,329 --> 00:41:41,248
Um, Arnaldo gave you this, didn't he?

724
00:41:41,916 --> 00:41:43,918
[ominous music playing]

725
00:41:44,001 --> 00:41:46,962
TRANSFER CERTIFICATE OF TITLE
EMILIA ARDIENTE TORILLO

726
00:41:47,046 --> 00:41:50,341
Arnaldo doesn't know that
Papa already gave that to me,

727
00:41:50,424 --> 00:41:52,676
so I had it transferred under my name.

728
00:41:54,220 --> 00:41:57,306
[in English] While the congressman
was in the hospital?

729
00:41:57,890 --> 00:42:00,226
How did that happen? Amazing.

730
00:42:00,935 --> 00:42:02,853
[in English] You know, Ivy,
when you're the governor,

731
00:42:02,937 --> 00:42:04,230
[in English] you can do
everything you want.

732
00:42:04,313 --> 00:42:06,357
You can raise the dead,

733
00:42:06,440 --> 00:42:08,150
or make the bedridden sign papers.

734
00:42:08,734 --> 00:42:09,944
[in English] Impressive, Emilia.

735
00:42:10,736 --> 00:42:14,949
Now I know how the
powerful get their hands

736
00:42:15,032 --> 00:42:16,700
on the land of the poor.

737
00:42:18,452 --> 00:42:20,788
Ivy, I didn't steal anything.

738
00:42:20,871 --> 00:42:22,164
I just made changes.

739
00:42:22,915 --> 00:42:24,124
You have a point.

740
00:42:24,833 --> 00:42:26,043
[in English] So,

741
00:42:26,794 --> 00:42:30,631
what can I do to get this land title?

742
00:42:31,340 --> 00:42:34,093
I already made a promise
to the poor farmers.

743
00:42:34,176 --> 00:42:36,220
And I don't want to embarrass myself.

744
00:42:37,054 --> 00:42:39,306
[in English] Oh, Ivy, another thing.

745
00:42:39,848 --> 00:42:41,183
Stay away from Arnaldo.

746
00:42:41,892 --> 00:42:43,936
[in English] You know that Arnaldo's
with Natalie, right?

747
00:42:47,690 --> 00:42:48,524
It's not my fault.

748
00:42:49,275 --> 00:42:51,360
You should talk to your son.

749
00:42:51,443 --> 00:42:52,736
Since he's the one…

750
00:42:54,113 --> 00:42:57,741
who keeps chasing after me.
It's getting annoying.

751
00:42:58,826 --> 00:42:59,660
Ivy,

752
00:42:59,743 --> 00:43:04,373
I know that Arnaldo wants you
to back him up in the Senate race.

753
00:43:04,456 --> 00:43:05,916
It's true, right?

754
00:43:06,000 --> 00:43:08,419
[in English] Honestly, I was hurt.

755
00:43:08,502 --> 00:43:10,838
Because you kept it a secret from me.

756
00:43:10,921 --> 00:43:12,590
[in English] I thought
you were loyal to me.

757
00:43:13,507 --> 00:43:15,050
[in English] I am, Emilia.

758
00:43:16,051 --> 00:43:18,554
[tense music playing]

759
00:43:18,637 --> 00:43:23,100
That's why I'm going to buy
your overpriced property.

760
00:43:25,811 --> 00:43:28,147
[in English] A hundred and fifty million.
Is that enough?

761
00:43:32,901 --> 00:43:34,111
[in English] How'd you know
that's what I wanted?

762
00:43:35,654 --> 00:43:38,365
Emilia… We're friends, aren't we?

763
00:43:39,074 --> 00:43:41,869
We know each other really well.
Anything else?

764
00:43:43,704 --> 00:43:46,707
[in English] Ivy, you know,
you're very generous.

765
00:43:47,458 --> 00:43:49,168
You're such a good friend.

766
00:43:49,251 --> 00:43:51,170
You give me everything I want.

767
00:43:53,631 --> 00:43:56,425
[in English] But…
Let me just remind you, Emilia…

768
00:43:57,426 --> 00:44:02,431
I don't like any of my friends
using me for my money.

769
00:44:03,015 --> 00:44:04,683
I'm sure you know that fake people…

770
00:44:05,684 --> 00:44:08,771
belong in the trash.

771
00:44:09,355 --> 00:44:10,898
[in English] How dare you?

772
00:44:12,066 --> 00:44:12,900
[in English] Natalie, stop.

773
00:44:12,983 --> 00:44:14,985
[in English] How can you let her
talk to you like that?

774
00:44:15,653 --> 00:44:18,072
[in English] [exhales]
Natalie, we're friends.

775
00:44:18,155 --> 00:44:19,198
That's how the two of us talk.

776
00:44:19,281 --> 00:44:21,033
[in English] We're very honest
with each other.

777
00:44:21,116 --> 00:44:23,827
[in English] Yes, and Emilia and I
respect each other,

778
00:44:23,911 --> 00:44:24,870
[in English] right?

779
00:44:24,953 --> 00:44:26,205
[in English] Yes, and…

780
00:44:26,288 --> 00:44:28,540
-[in English] we fear each other, right?
-No.

781
00:44:30,376 --> 00:44:31,752
I'm not afraid of you.

782
00:44:31,835 --> 00:44:34,171
[tense music playing]

783
00:44:35,464 --> 00:44:39,134
Because I know
you could never hurt me, Emilia.

784
00:44:42,054 --> 00:44:43,472
And that goes for me too.

785
00:44:49,937 --> 00:44:51,480
[in English] Shall we eat?

786
00:44:51,563 --> 00:44:53,190
[tense music continues playing]

787
00:45:05,285 --> 00:45:06,620
[Pandoy clears throat]

788
00:45:07,830 --> 00:45:09,289
-Auntie…
-[snorts]

789
00:45:09,373 --> 00:45:10,707
I'm so happy.

790
00:45:10,791 --> 00:45:11,708
[stifled laughter]

791
00:45:11,792 --> 00:45:14,545
-You don't say?
-I can see that.

792
00:45:14,628 --> 00:45:17,256
Why don't you try keeping
that smile of yours

793
00:45:17,339 --> 00:45:19,633
from reaching the top of your head?

794
00:45:19,716 --> 00:45:21,468
[laughing]

795
00:45:21,552 --> 00:45:22,928
Well? Have you confessed yet?

796
00:45:23,011 --> 00:45:24,346
Are you going to court her?

797
00:45:26,306 --> 00:45:27,433
Uh…

798
00:45:28,642 --> 00:45:29,685
Uh?

799
00:45:30,227 --> 00:45:32,354
-[Loring] Eh?
-[laughing]

800
00:45:35,566 --> 00:45:38,652
[ominous music playing]

801
00:45:48,745 --> 00:45:52,416
[Arnaldo] <i>I won't let Diego</i>
<i>steal Ivy from me.</i>

802
00:45:52,499 --> 00:45:55,335
[ominous music playing]

803
00:45:55,419 --> 00:45:56,545
[panicked breathing]

804
00:45:58,755 --> 00:46:00,507
Sir, please have mercy.

805
00:46:00,591 --> 00:46:02,259
I'm losing my mind here!

806
00:46:02,342 --> 00:46:04,261
I'm easy to talk to.

807
00:46:04,344 --> 00:46:06,138
[panicked breathing]

808
00:46:07,556 --> 00:46:10,350
I know you're thirsty. How about a drink?

809
00:46:10,434 --> 00:46:11,685
-Yes, sir.
-Here.

810
00:46:17,983 --> 00:46:18,817
Oh, it's all out.

811
00:46:23,197 --> 00:46:24,573
[man] Boss, here's his food.

812
00:46:26,867 --> 00:46:27,868
[Jepoy] Let him eat.

813
00:46:27,951 --> 00:46:31,205
[ominous music playing]

814
00:46:35,125 --> 00:46:36,293
[grunts]

815
00:46:37,419 --> 00:46:38,420
[groans]

816
00:46:38,504 --> 00:46:40,297
Hey. Hey!

817
00:46:41,340 --> 00:46:42,549
It's okay.

818
00:46:43,300 --> 00:46:45,052
He won't get far.

819
00:46:45,135 --> 00:46:47,387
[Raul] That's what
I'm hoping for, Senator.

820
00:46:47,971 --> 00:46:49,765
I want to resume our gambling operations.

821
00:46:49,848 --> 00:46:51,683
I'm just waiting for your blessing.

822
00:46:52,559 --> 00:46:54,520
I've been wanting to resume them too.

823
00:46:54,603 --> 00:46:59,233
I just can't find anyone I can trust.

824
00:46:59,316 --> 00:47:02,110
We go way back, right, Senator?

825
00:47:02,194 --> 00:47:04,071
You can leave me in charge.

826
00:47:04,780 --> 00:47:07,366
-[in English] I trust you, Raul.
-Thank you.

827
00:47:07,449 --> 00:47:10,285
But after what happened--

828
00:47:10,369 --> 00:47:12,371
I know I need to be extra careful.

829
00:47:12,454 --> 00:47:14,331
That's what I'll do, Senator.

830
00:47:14,414 --> 00:47:16,458
[in English] I hope you could
give me a chance,

831
00:47:16,542 --> 00:47:19,461
and I'll be hugely indebted to you.

832
00:47:20,212 --> 00:47:21,255
Okay.

833
00:47:23,173 --> 00:47:24,967
Does Emilia know about this?

834
00:47:25,759 --> 00:47:27,844
I don't think she needs to know.

835
00:47:29,763 --> 00:47:32,975
[phone ringing]

836
00:47:33,058 --> 00:47:34,101
AUNT BELEN

837
00:47:34,184 --> 00:47:36,770
[in English] Excuse me, Senator.
I need to take this.

838
00:47:37,896 --> 00:47:39,106
[Raul exhales]

839
00:47:40,440 --> 00:47:41,567
-Hello, Auntie?
-Raul,

840
00:47:41,650 --> 00:47:43,443
you need to get back here right now.

841
00:47:43,527 --> 00:47:45,279
Why, Auntie? What happened to her?

842
00:47:48,699 --> 00:47:50,701
I think she's coming back to her senses.

843
00:47:50,784 --> 00:47:53,954
[tense music playing]

844
00:48:10,220 --> 00:48:12,681
[tense music continues]

845
00:48:26,945 --> 00:48:29,156
Raul, are you going somewhere?

846
00:48:30,282 --> 00:48:32,117
[in English] Does Emilia know about this?

847
00:48:33,910 --> 00:48:35,329
[in English] I'm sorry, I have to do this.

848
00:48:36,246 --> 00:48:37,748
[in English] This is for your own good.

849
00:48:38,624 --> 00:48:41,001
-[in English] Guards!
-Yes, ma'am?

850
00:48:41,084 --> 00:48:42,502
Try to stop me,

851
00:48:43,337 --> 00:48:45,213
and you'll get what you're asking for!

852
00:48:46,882 --> 00:48:48,467
Where are you going?

853
00:48:48,550 --> 00:48:50,802
[tense music playing]

854
00:48:51,845 --> 00:48:53,472
You need money, right?

855
00:48:53,555 --> 00:48:55,474
So, I'm gonna take care
of our gambling business.

856
00:48:55,557 --> 00:48:57,309
The senator already gave me the go signal.

857
00:48:57,392 --> 00:49:00,729
I don't care if the devil himself
gave you the go.

858
00:49:00,812 --> 00:49:03,065
If I tell you to stay,
you're going to stay.

859
00:49:03,565 --> 00:49:04,608
And I don't need money anymore…

860
00:49:04,691 --> 00:49:06,234
-I have a lot of that!
-Stop it, Emilia.

861
00:49:07,277 --> 00:49:09,613
If I want to leave this house,
then I will!

862
00:49:13,075 --> 00:49:15,535
Raul. Raul!

863
00:49:15,619 --> 00:49:16,703
Raul!

864
00:49:21,083 --> 00:49:23,919
[tense music playing]

865
00:49:25,212 --> 00:49:27,255
<i>-Lily, help me.</i>
<i>-Mom.</i>

866
00:49:29,216 --> 00:49:30,550
<i>Mom!</i>

867
00:49:30,634 --> 00:49:31,968
[Ivy] <i>Jepoy, this feels different.</i>

868
00:49:32,052 --> 00:49:34,763
<i>I want to make sure my mom really is dead.</i>

869
00:49:34,846 --> 00:49:36,348
<i>Tomorrow's the announcement, Senator.</i>

870
00:49:36,431 --> 00:49:38,475
<i>Are you ready to go</i>
<i>against your own mother?</i>

871
00:49:38,558 --> 00:49:40,477
[Raul] <i>The higher your dreams are,</i>

872
00:49:40,560 --> 00:49:42,562
<i>the harder you'll fall.</i>

873
00:49:42,646 --> 00:49:44,481
[in English] <i>I am Emilia Ardiente,</i>

874
00:49:44,564 --> 00:49:45,899
[in English] <i>destined to be a queen,</i>

875
00:49:45,982 --> 00:49:48,276
[in English] <i>and my reign starts today.</i>

876
00:49:48,360 --> 00:49:50,028
[in English]<i> I'm proud to present to you</i>

877
00:49:50,112 --> 00:49:52,948
<i>the person who will complete</i>
<i>the senatorial line up,</i>

878
00:49:53,031 --> 00:49:55,117
[in English] <i>a prolific leader,</i>

879
00:49:55,200 --> 00:49:56,702
<i>none other than…</i>

880
00:49:58,203 --> 00:50:00,247
[theme music playing]
